From: Jonathan Schwender <55576758+jschwe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:28:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] script: Fix TimerListener leak (#48752)

Fixes a leak, where the Trusted reference would keep windows alive until
the Timer expires.
Looking up the global via the pipelineId avoids this. For workers we can
keep the direct reference since the timer scheduler is owned by the
worker, hence if that is dropped, so is the reference.

Testing: We don't have automated tests to prevent leaks.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 5f65837a45d56f857c099e8c640dbf317ab4a0d1)

----

Fork note: backport of upstream 5f65837a45d (#48752, fixes upstream
issue 48741), which landed after base/2026-10-08. A window or iframe
that is discarded while it has a pending timer stays alive, with its
whole JS heap, until the timer would have fired. The upstream message
above lacks its `Fixes:` line, so that it does not reference an issue of
this repo, and its empty squash-merge separator.
Drop at the next sync: every later base contains 5f65837a45d, so this
commit applies empty and becomes a `Superseded-by: 5f65837a45d`
placeholder (runbook decision 3).

Validation: Release builds of ohos-main plus patch 48 alone and plus patches 47 and 48, headless servoshell with `--pref=dom_testutils_enabled=true`, two runs each. A page that adds and removes same-origin iframes and counts, after `TestUtils.gc()`, the removed documents still alive through WeakRefs: 20 iframes each with a pending 100 s timer, 20/20 alive without this patch and 0/20 with it; 40 iframes running a typical page (DOM, listeners, observers, a timer, promises, fonts, canvas, messaging), 40/40 alive at 571 MiB RSS without it and 0/40 at 299 MiB with it. WPT with patches 47 to 49: `./mach test-wpt --release --processes 6 html/webappapis/timers html/browsers/browsing-the-web html/browsers/history page-visibility performance-timeline js workers html/webappapis/scripting/event-loops user-timing` (1029 tests): 1023 as expected. The other 6 are flaky or broken on plain ohos-main too (A/B repeats, plain ohos-main vs with the patches): navigation-unload-same-origin-fragment.html FAIL 6/10 vs 7/10; cross-origin-top-navigation-with-user-activation-in-parent.window.html TIMEOUT 23/30 vs 29/30 (18/20 vs 20/20 in the interleaved rounds); location_replace_session_history.html (expected TIMEOUT) ends in ERROR, TIMEOUT or CRASH on both, 28/2/0 vs 22/5/3 of 30; same-document-refresh.html PASS 9/10 vs 10/10 (stale FAIL expectation); form-submit-cross-frame.html FAIL 2/10 vs 0/10; iframe-src-204.html FAIL once in the full run, 0/10 vs 0/10 in repeats. `./mach fmt` and `./mach test-tidy` are clean.
